    "model": "# This is the WinBUGS version of the DUGONGS  model, without discretization\n# of the variable gamma (This was done due to a technical limitation of\n# classic BUGS: it could only sample from log concave distributions)\n#\nvar\n   x[N],Y[N],mu[N],alpha,beta,gamma,tau,sigma,p[M],U1,U2,U3;\nmodel {\n   for (i in 1:N) {\n      mu[i] <- alpha - beta * gamma^x[i]\n      Y[i] ~ dnorm(mu[i], tau)\n   }\n   alpha ~ dnorm(0.0, 1.0E-6) \n   beta ~ dnorm(0.0, 1.0E-6) \n   gamma ~ dunif(0.5, 1)\n   tau ~ dgamma(1.0E-3, 1.0E-3)\n   sigma <- 1.0/sqrt(tau)\n   U3 <- logit(gamma)\n}\n\n# rjags reference summary (seed=1234; chains=2; n.adapt=1000; burnin=5000; n.iter=5000; thin=1)\n# parameter                         mean          sd        q2.5         q50       q97.5    n\n# U3                                1.8788     0.27375      1.3147      1.8919      2.3882 10000\n# alpha                             2.6570    0.072474      2.5286      2.6516      2.8159 10000\n# beta                             0.97374    0.076939     0.82741     0.97256      1.1278 10000\n# gamma                            0.86431    0.033318     0.78830     0.86897     0.91593 10000\n# sigma                           0.099203    0.015099    0.074935    0.097452     0.13390 10000",
